## Interpretation

After correction, the baseline and receptor-informed models differed only in `DCM.M.pE.G`. The corrected receptor-informed model had a free-energy advantage of approximately `62.20` over the matched zero-centred baseline, indicating substantially greater model evidence for the receptor-informed G prior means in this fitted model.

The earlier receptor-informed inversion (`F ≈ -397.88`) should not be used for scientific interpretation because the model also differed in `pC.D`. The corrected inversion supersedes that result.

**Caution:** The inversion log reached iteration 64. The finite free energy and posterior estimates were saved successfully, but convergence diagnostics and identical inversion settings across models should be documented before treating the comparison as final.

